# Post Processing's tonemap chain on D3D11 (0) or the render graph (1): Whiterun at 13:00 in clear weather, then
# Dragonsreach, a shot of each.
# Effects the graph runs: Vignette, Color Grading and Tone Mapping, LUT, Border, Camera, Motion Blur, Composite.
# CS_PP_ONLY forces which sub-effects are on for the whole run, every frame, over SettingsUser.json and the scene blends
# (which re-apply Post Processing's settings every frame); the others are off, and Composite turns itself off with no
# contributor. The log line "[PostProcessing] CS_PP_ONLY: only these sub-features are on ..." confirms it. Add a name
# (the sub-effect's type, e.g. "COD Bloom") once its port is merged.
# Optional, in SettingsUser.json under "PostProcessing":
#   "Border": { "settings": { "Scale": [0.1, 0.1, 0.0, 0.0], "BorderColor": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0] } }   (a visible letterbox)
#   "LUT" with an empty "LutPath" draws nothing on either path; set a .dds/.png LUT to test it.
# Camera's film grain follows the frame count, so the two paths' shots differ by grain noise.
# Effects11 must not own the tonemap (its effect off), or Post Processing does not run at all.
# Without CS_PP_ONLY (the default sub-effects on), CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=1 logs "[ORG] Post Processing: the chain runs on D3D11: ..."
# naming each one without an ORG implementation, and the frame matches D3D11.
CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=1
CS_PP_ONLY=Vignette,Color Grading and Tone Mapping,LUT,Border,Camera,Motion Blur
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2500:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3600:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3700
